id=a52sxq_resolution_quickpanel
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: quick panel keeps its geometry with Display > Screen resolution
author=kusti420
description=UNTESTED-ON-DEVICE. SystemUI's "scaling adjustment" (communal DensityUtils: getInitialDisplayDensity / getBaseDisplayDensity, reused by the One UI 9 Compose quick panel as LocalScaleAdjustment, clamped to 0.95..1.21) is meant to cancel Screen zoom. A forced display size also lowers the base density (450 -> 300 -> 225) while the initial density stays 450, so the big (bar) tile icons became 48dp x 1.21 (109 px instead of 90 at HD+, 82 instead of 68 at 540p; measured with resaudit), their labels moved right and got clipped, tile outlines 1.5x / 2x. The ratio is now taken relative to the default density of the current resolution (initialDensity x baseWidth / (baseDensity x initialWidth)): 1.0 at all three resolutions, Screen zoom still cancelled. Two raw pixel constants in the tile code (50 px label inset, 20 px row slide-in) are converted to dp.
